  "notes": "はぐらかす describes a deliberate evasion — not through refusal, but through skillful redirection or vagueness.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n- Pattern: 〜をはぐらかす\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {質問|しつもん}をはぐらかす (to dodge a question)\n- {話題|わだい}をはぐらかす (to deflect a topic)\n- {話|はなし}をはぐらかす (to evade a conversation)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ごまかす: to cover up, to gloss over (broader, includes deception)\n- はぐらかす: to dodge, to evade (specifically about deflecting questions/topics)\n- {逃|に}げる: to run away (physical or figurative escape)\n\nUSAGE: Often used with a slightly negative connotation, suggesting the person is being evasive or uncooperative.",
